# pband_bw run matrix  (read by scripts/launch.sh)
#
# Multi-PC p-band steering (ATTACK_METHODOLOGY.md 4b). One mixed-predictability
# victim on core 0, co-located against a BINARY attacker switch (idle / heavy) on
# core 1, crossed with the aware (reward live) and blind (reward inert) configs.
# 2 neighbors x 2 configs = 4 runs.
#
#   victim   <source>                 [prog-args...]
#   neighbor <name> <source>          [prog-args...]
#   config   <name> <ini>
#
# Output .out files are named <neighbor>_<config>.out (consumed by rollup.py).
# rollup.py also reads build/pband_bw_victim.out (via nm) to map trigger PCs to the
# victim's pband_pc_<j> load sites.

victim   victim.c

# Binary switch: intermediate duties give no gradation (bucket saturates at <5% duty).
neighbor atk_idle      attacker.c      idle
neighbor atk_heavy     attacker.c      heavy

# aware = HBW reward table live (attack); blind = reward table inert (isolation).
# Both pin the HBW degree curve EQUAL to normal and enable the per-PC counter.
config   aware   aware.ini
config   blind   blind.ini
